;; Endeavor 142 Phase B CAPSTONE (part 1) — a runtime-K register-ring matmul, auto-unrolled.
;; The K-loop uses the SAME idiom as the SLM scratch ring (topology.md ~L950): a plain dotimes whose
;; ring-get slot is (mod grid-k RING-COUNT).  Because the ring here is a REGISTER ring (GRF, not runtime-
;; indexable), the compiler UNROLLS the loop by :ring-count so each copy's slot folds to a compile-time
;; literal (copy j -> slot j) — the double-buffer becomes ring-count independent fragment-var sets.  Data
;; coords keep the absolute K block (grid-k + j).  n-k-steps is RUNTIME ((inner-dimension A B) / tile-K),
;; so this proves the general runtime-K path, not a hand-unrolled constant.
;;
;; This first capstone verifies CORRECTNESS (C = sum_k A[k].B[k]) with the ring rotating across K; the
;; prefetch-overlapped / benchmarked pipeline is the next step (it decides the Subgroup2DBlockLoad swap).
;; Requires n-k-steps divisible by :ring-count (v1 contract; K is always a multiple of the tile-K).
;;
;; COMPILE-WITH[--hardware-profile=bmg --ir-target=spv]: PASS
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS
;; SKIP-WITH[--differentiate]: "COMPILES, but the gradient is WRONG — measured, not assumed, and characterised.  The over-count factor is (K+1): analytical=10.8 vs FD=1.199 at K=8, and analytical=39.6 vs FD=1.195 at K=32.  The finite difference matches hand-computation both times, so the FORWARD is right and the BACKWARD adds a spurious term proportional to K.  RULED OUT: ring slot REUSE — a single-k-step variant (K=8, one iteration, no slot shared) is already 9x wrong.  ALSO VERIFIED CORRECT by reading the emitted backward: the dA loop reads B at (grid-k*8 + k, n), and %load-tile-at-bwd scatters the slot to A_GRAD at (0, grid-k*8) — per-iteration math and coordinates both check out.  So the defect is elsewhere and the (K+1) shape is the clue.  SEPARATE REAL DEFECT found while looking, worth fixing regardless: the ring adjoint slot is never RESET between iterations that share it (slot 0 serves grid-k 0 and 2), which is BUG 036's shape one level up; it corrupts other columns even though it does not explain dA[0,0]."
;;
;; Endeavor 146: the old reason read "forward-only ring / MMA".  False on both halves — MMA
;; differentiates (142/01, 145/12) and ring staging differentiates (145/18).  What actually
;; blocked this spec was NOT an AD gap at all: `(mod grid-k 2)` failed with
;;     Type mismatch for operator '/'. Cannot operate on ULONG and INT.
;; because analyze-mod-expression expanded to (- x (* (/ x y) y)) WITHOUT coercing, and a Lisp
;; integer literal reads as INT while grid-k is ULONG.  A pure FORWARD bug — it reproduces in a
;; four-line kernel with no --differentiate.  The forward here escaped it only because the ring
;; index is unrolled at compile time, so the mod never reached the analyzer; adding the backward
;; is what first made it reach.  Fixed in analyze-mod-expression by coercing a LITERAL divisor
;; to the dividend's type (variables still error, which is where strictness earns its keep).
;;
;; THE CHECK IS LEFT IN PLACE THOUGH THE SPEC IS SKIPPED, because it is the thing that found
;; the defect and it will be the thing that confirms the fix.  142/01 proves register-resident
;; MMA and 145/18 proves ring STAGING; their COMBINATION — a k-loop over a register-tile ring
;; feeding MMA — is what is still unproven, and now known WRONG rather than merely unproven.
;; f(A,B) = sum(A.B) with K=32, so
;; dA[m,k] = sum_n B[k,n]; with B[i][j] = 0.01*(i*16+j), dA[0,0] = 0.01 * sum_{n=0..15} n = 1.2.
;; VERIFY-AUTODIFF: A=16x32@0:0.01 B=32x16@0:0.01 at.A=0,0 expect.A=1.2 group=16 h=0.5 atol=2e-2 output-mat=16x16
;; SKIP-WITH[--debug]: "pre-existing --debug c-t-accessor codegen bug (plan/bugs.md #033)"
;;
;; On-metal correctness (host-reference C = A.B, K=32 = four 8-wide K-blocks -> n-k-steps=4, so the
;; unrolled-by-2 loop runs 2 outer iterations: proves multi-iteration accumulation, not a 1-trip fold):
;; MMA-DIMS: 16 16 32
;; HOIST-HARDWARE-PROFILE: bmg
;; TEST-HOIST[L0]: validate-l0-mma-run
;; HOIST-EXPECT: MMA_CORRECT

(def-hardware-profile bmg :simd-width 16 :mma-shapes ((8 16 8)))

(def-type a-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type b-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type c-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel matmul (A B &out C)
  (declare #'(a-mat b-mat &out c-mat)
           (global-size :set-to 16) (local-size :set-to 16))
  (let ((A-ring (make-register-tile-ring float (16 8) :ring-count 2 :operand :a))
        (B-ring (make-register-tile-ring float (8 16) :ring-count 2 :operand :b))
        (C-tile (make-register-tile float (16 16) 0.0))
        (n-k-steps (/ (inner-dimension A B) (to-ulong 8))))   ; K / tile-K  (runtime ulong)
    (dotimes (grid-k n-k-steps)
      ;; slot = (mod grid-k 2) — the compiler unrolls by 2 so this is static per copy
      (load-tile A (ring-get A-ring (mod grid-k 2)) (0 grid-k))
      (load-tile B (ring-get B-ring (mod grid-k 2)) (grid-k 0))
      (mma-accumulate-via-tile (8 16 8) C-tile
                               (ring-get A-ring (mod grid-k 2))
                               (ring-get B-ring (mod grid-k 2))))
    (store-tile C-tile C (0 0))))
